## 1. Abstract

This project builds an end-to-end Natural Language Processing (NLP) application. Text is cleaned, split into subword tokens (BPE and WordPiece), converted into vectors (TF-IDF, Word2Vec, BERT), compared with cosine similarity, and classified into news topics by two approaches: a trained TF-IDF + Logistic Regression model and a Groq-hosted LLM using zero-shot and few-shot prompting. All functions are exposed through a tested FastAPI service. The trained classifier reaches **97.4% accuracy** on the 426-article test set.

