## 12. Challenges and Solutions

| Challenge | Solution |
|---|---|
| Package install failed on Python 3.13 (`gensim` needs an older NumPy) | Word2Vec is trained on Colab and saved as `.npy` + `.json`; the API loads it without `gensim` |
| BERT is slow on a normal computer | Document vectors are precomputed on a Colab GPU; only the query is encoded live |
| Groq model `llama-3.1-8b-instant` was retired (16 Aug 2026) | Switched to `openai/gpt-oss-20b`; the model is a setting (`GROQ_MODEL`) |
| LLM returned empty answers with `max_tokens=10` | Raised to 300 and set `reasoning_effort` to low, because the model thinks before answering |
| Free-tier limit of 8,000 tokens per minute | Smaller prompts, a 50-article sample and pauses between calls |
| Missing files or keys could crash the API | Custom errors return readable 503 messages |

## 13. Limitations and Future Work

- BPE and WordPiece are teaching versions, slower than Hugging Face `tokenizers`.
- BBC News has five clean topics, so scores are higher than on noisy real-world data.
- LLM evaluation uses a small sample because of free-tier limits.
- BERT input is cut to 256 tokens.

**Future work:** Docker container, fine-tuning BERT for classification, a vector index for faster search, API authentication and rate limiting, and cross-validation.

## 14. Conclusion

The project covers the whole path from raw text to a working application. Text is cleaned, tokenized with two subword methods, vectorized in three ways, compared with cosine similarity and classified by both a trained model and an LLM, all behind a tested and documented FastAPI service. The classic TF-IDF + Logistic Regression model performs very well on this dataset (97.4% accuracy), and the LLM comparison will complete the evaluation once the corrected run is finished. Beyond the technical result, the project gave practical experience in how real NLP systems are built, evaluated, packaged and delivered.

## 15. Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Token | A small unit of text (word, subword or character) |
| Vocabulary | All tokens a tokenizer or model knows |
| Out-of-vocabulary | A word never seen during training |
| Subword | A frequent word piece such as `##ball` |
| Embedding / vector | A list of numbers representing a text or word |
| Sparse / dense vector | Mostly zeros (TF-IDF) / all positions filled (Word2Vec, BERT) |
| Cosine similarity | Score for how close the direction of two vectors is |
| Supervised learning | Learning from examples with correct labels |
| Zero-shot / few-shot | Asking an LLM to do a task with no examples / a few examples |
| Prompt | The instruction text given to an LLM |
| Confusion matrix | Table of true versus predicted classes |
| Pickle / joblib | Saving a Python object to a file |
| Endpoint | A URL of the API that performs one function |
| Rate limit | Maximum number of API calls or tokens per time period |
